    <docsection name="ags_playback">
      <doc xml:space="preserve"
           filename="audio/ags_playback.c"
           line="47">#AgsPlayback represents a context to output. It provides you the channel processing threads
per #AgsSoundScope-enum.

The assigned #AgsChannelThread calls ags_channel_recursive_run_stage() for you.</doc>
    </docsection>
    <docsection name="ags_playback_domain">
      <doc xml:space="preserve"
           filename="audio/ags_playback_domain.c"
           line="49">#AgsPlaybackDomain represents a domain to output. It provides you the audio processing threads
per #AgsSoundScope-enum. The

The assigned #AgsAudioThread calls ags_channel_recursive_run_stage() for you.

The `output-playback` and `input-playback` properties provide a #GList-struct containing #AgsPlayback.</doc>
    </docsection>
    <docsection name="ags_plugin_port">
      <doc xml:space="preserve"
           filename="plugin/ags_plugin_port.c"
           line="40">The #AgsPluginPort describes a plugin's port. For real ports used by the
processing tree please take a look at #AgsPort.</doc>
    </docsection>
    <docsection name="ags_port">
      <doc xml:space="preserve"
           filename="audio/ags_port.c"
           line="63">#AgsPort provides a thread-safe way to access or change values or properties.

The `specifier` property has to be unique within context.

You call ags_port_safe_write() to alter a value or ags_port_safe_read() to read a
port.</doc>
    </docsection>
    <docsection name="ags_port_util">
      <doc xml:space="preserve"
           filename="audio/ags_port_util.c"
           line="38">Utility functions to deal with #AgsPort.</doc>
    </docsection>
